jobs.description:
SamenvattingStart as an Orderpicker in Woerden and help keep Jumbo stores stocked across the Netherlands. Earn up to €23.39 gross per hour, and enjoy a hands-on logistics job with clear routines and a supportive team. No specific education required, just motivation and a willingness to learn. Good work!Over de functieAs an Orderpicker, you’ll prepare orders for Jumbo stores across the Netherlands using a modern voice-pick system. Depending on the assignment, you will work in a warm (+18°C) or chilled (+2°C to +4°C) area at the warehouse.

Your tasks:
-  Picking orders with a voice-pick system;
-  Placing products on trolleys or pallets;
-  Checking orders for accuracy and quality;
-  Keeping your workspace clean and organized;
-  Following warehouse and safety procedures;

This job is for 32–40 hours per week in a two-shift system, with occasional weekend work.
The worktimes are from 06.00 - 14:00 and 14.00 - 21:00.
Over het bedrijfAt Jumbo’s distribution centre in Woerden, teamwork keeps things moving. Every day, colleagues work together to prepare orders and make sure stores across the Netherlands receive the groceries and everyday products their customers need. You will join a modern, well-organized workplace where everyone plays a part. Clear procedures, a focus on quality and helpful colleagues make it a great place to gain experience in logistics and develop your skills.
Wat wij vragen- Own accommodation in The Netherlands. For this job we don't provide housing;
- Basic English skills to understand instructions and communicate with your team
- Willingness to work in warm and chilled areas;
- Physically stable and comfortable with walking and lifting during the shift;
- You are available to work in 2-shifts.

Of course, these points are essential for the role of order picker, but we are primarily interested in who you are! Inspire us.
Wat wij bieden- A salary between €14.99 and €15.21 gross per hour for work in the warm warehouse and €15.37–€15.59

SamenvattingStart as an Order Picker in Nieuwegein and make sure Albert Heijn supermarkets receive their products on time. Earn €14.99 gross per hour and allowances for working in shifts. Stay active throughout your working day, work with a friendly team, and make a difference every day. Good work!Over de functieAs an Orderpicker at this logistics organization in Nieuwegein, you make sure supermarkets receive their fresh products every day. Using a modern voice-picking system, available in Dutch, English, Polish, and Ukrainian, you collect orders in the warehouse. You walk a lot, pick products from shelves, and prepare orders for transport. You work quickly and accurately, because the stores depend on you. The job takes place in a refrigerated environment (around 4°C), so it’s important you are comfortable with cooler temperatures. You’ll receive clear instructions through the voice-picking system so you know exactly which products to collect.
Your tasks:
- Collecting products using a voice-picking system;
- Preparing and organizing trolleys for shipment;
- Checking product quantities and quality.

This job is for 40 hours per week. Your shifts will be scheduled as follows:
- Morning shift: 05:00–14:30
- Night shift: 19:30–04:00

Over het bedrijfAt your new workplace in Nieuwegein, you’ll work alongside colleagues from different countries towards one shared goal: making sure supermarkets across the Netherlands receive their fresh products on time. The atmosphere is friendly and welcoming. Colleagues help each other when needed, chat during breaks, and always have time for a joke. Together, you contribute to something that people rely on every day.
Wat wij vragen- You have your own accomodation in The Netherlands. For this job we don't provide housing;
- You speak Dutch, English, or Polish;
- You’re physically fit and able to perform physical work;
- You’re comfortable working in a chilled environment (around 4°C);
- You’re flexible and willing to work week

What will you be doing?
As a Production Employee, you play an important role in the preparation and packaging of food products. Together with your team, you help keep production running efficiently while making sure quality and safety standards are met. Your attention to detail and proactive attitude contribute to a smooth workflow and a well-organized production environment.

Your responsibilities include:

• Packing and preparing finished products so they are ready for shipment;
• Setting up, operating, and monitoring production equipment during the manufacturing process;
• Performing quality checks on products, packaging, and labeling to ensure all requirements are met;
• Keeping the work area clean, tidy, and compliant with hygiene and safety regulations;
• Collaborating with colleagues and supervisors to achieve production goals and meet daily schedules.

Functie-eisen:
What are we looking for?

• You have a good command of either English, Dutch, or both, allowing you to understand procedures and work safely within a production environment;
• You enjoy working in different locations and are open to being assigned to various production facilities throughout the region;
• You are flexible regarding working hours and can work rotating shifts, including mornings, afternoons, evenings, and nights for 16 to 32 hours per week;
• You are eager to learn new skills, adapt quickly to changing tasks, and become familiar with different production equipment;
• You have an eye for detail, value quality, and actively contribute to a clean, organized, and safe workplace.
